---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../../styles/global.css";
---

<Layout
	title="Applications & Solved NCERT Problems | Class 10 | The Concepts Adda"
	description="Master exam-focused NCERT word problems involving medicine capsules, 2 joined cubes, pen stand depressions, and hollow vessels for Class 10 Mathematics."
>
	<main class="lesson-page">
		<div class="lesson-container">
			<a href="/surface-areas-and-volumes" class="back-link">
				<span class="back-arrow">←</span>
				<span>Back to Surface Areas & Volumes</span>
			</a>

			<!-- LESSON HEADER -->
			<section class="lesson-header">
				<div class="lesson-number">03</div>
				<div class="lesson-header-copy">
					<div class="lesson-label">LESSON 03 · CLASS 10 MATHEMATICS (NCERT)</div>
					<h1>Applications & Solved <span>NCERT Problems</span></h1>
					<p>
						Master exam-focused NCERT word problems involving medicine capsules, joined cubes, pen stand depressions, and hollow vessels with 3D SVG diagrams.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- CONTENT LAYOUT -->
			<section class="content-layout">
				<article class="lesson-content">

					<!-- 01 · STRATEGY -->
					<div class="topic-label">01 · EXAM STRATEGY</div>
					<h2>Solving Complex Combined Shapes</h2>

					<div class="summary-list">
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>Step 1</span>
							<p>Break the composite object into standard geometric solids (Cylinder, Cone, Hemisphere, Cube).</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>Step 2</span>
							<p>For <strong>Surface Area</strong>: Add exposed CSA of all outer parts. For <strong>Volume</strong>: Add (or subtract) volumes directly.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>Step 3</span>
							<p>Factor out common terms like <strong>πr</strong> or <strong>r²</strong> before calculating to avoid arithmetic mistakes!</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 02 · SOLVED NCERT EXAMPLES -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">02 · SOLVED NCERT EXAMPLES</div>
					<h2>Step-by-Step Problem Solving</h2>

					<!-- Example 1 -->
					<div class="example-card">
						<div class="example-header">
							<span class="example-badge">EXAMPLE 1 · MEDICINE CAPSULE</span>
							<h3>A medicine capsule is in the shape of a cylinder with two hemispheres stuck to each of its ends. The length of the entire capsule is 14 mm and diameter is 5 mm. Find its surface area.</h3>
						</div>
						<div class="example-solution">
							<!-- SVG Diagram -->
							<div style="margin:15px 0; text-align:center;">
								<svg width="360" height="180" viewBox="0 0 360 180" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="background:#f8fafc; border-radius:18px; border:1px solid #cbd5e1; box-shadow:0 6px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.03);">
									<!-- Capsule Body -->
									<rect x="110" y="55" width="140" height="70" fill="#eff6ff" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="2.5"/>

									<!-- Left Hemispherical Cap -->
									<path d="M 110,55 A 35 35 0 0 0 110,125 Z" fill="#dbeafe" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="2.5"/>

									<!-- Right Hemispherical Cap -->
									<path d="M 250,55 A 35 35 0 0 1 250,125 Z" fill="#dbeafe" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="2.5"/>

									<!-- Dashed Junction Ellipses -->
									<ellipse cx="110" cy="90" rx="8" ry="35" fill="none" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="3,3"/>
									<ellipse cx="250" cy="90" rx="8" ry="35" fill="none" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="3,3"/>

									<!-- Dimension Lines -->
									<line x1="75" y1="150" x2="285" y2="150" stroke="#0f172a" stroke-width="1.5"/>
									<text x="140" y="168" fill="#0f172a" font-size="13" font-weight="900">Total Length = 14 mm</text>

									<!-- Diameter Line -->
									<line x1="55" y1="55" x2="55" y2="125" stroke="#dc2626" stroke-width="1.5"/>
									<text x="15" y="95" fill="#dc2626" font-size="12" font-weight="900">5 mm</text>

									<!-- Labels -->
									<text x="135" y="95" fill="#2563eb" font-size="13" font-weight="900">Cylinder (h = 9 mm)</text>
									<text x="120" y="45" fill="#2563eb" font-size="11" font-weight="800">r = 2.5 mm</text>
								</svg>
							</div>

							<p>Diameter = 5 mm ⟹ Radius <em>r = 2.5 mm</em>.</p>
							<p>Height of cylinder <em>h = 14 - 2(2.5) = 14 - 5 = 9 mm</em>.</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								Surface Area = CSA of Cylinder + 2 × (CSA of Hemisphere)<br/>
								Surface Area = 2πrh + 2 × (2πr²) = 2πr (h + 2r)<br/>
								Surface Area = 2 × (22/7) × 2.5 × (9 + 5)<br/>
								Surface Area = 2 × (22/7) × 2.5 × 14 = 2 × 22 × 2.5 × 2 = <strong>220 mm²</strong>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- Example 2 -->
					<div class="example-card">
						<div class="example-header">
							<span class="example-badge">EXAMPLE 2 · TWO JOINED CUBES</span>
							<h3>2 cubes each of volume 64 cm³ are joined end to end. Find the surface area of the resulting cuboid.</h3>
						</div>
						<div class="example-solution">
							<p>Volume of cube <em>a³ = 64 cm³ ⟹ side a = 4 cm</em>.</p>
							<p>When two cubes are joined end to end:</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								Length of Cuboid l = 4 + 4 = <strong>8 cm</strong><br/>
								Breadth b = <strong>4 cm</strong><br/>
								Height h = <strong>4 cm</strong>
							</div>

							<p style="margin-top:14px;"><strong>Surface Area of Cuboid</strong>:</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								TSA = 2(lb + bh + hl)<br/>
								TSA = 2[(8 × 4) + (4 × 4) + (4 × 8)]<br/>
								TSA = 2(32 + 16 + 32) = 2(80) = <strong>160 cm²</strong>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 03 · QUICK SUMMARY -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">03 · QUICK SUMMARY</div>
					<h2>Key Takeaways</h2>

					<div class="summary-list">
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>01</span>
							<p>Capsule surface area = <strong>2πr (h + 2r)</strong>.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>02</span>
							<p>When cubes are joined end to end, only the <strong>length doubles</strong> (breadth and height stay same!).</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>03</span>
							<p>For pen stand conical depressions, <strong>subtract cone volumes</strong> from cuboid volume.</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- LESSON NAVIGATION -->
					<div class="lesson-navigation">
						<a href="/surface-areas-and-volumes/volume-of-combined-solids" class="previous-lesson">
							<span>←</span>
							<div>
								<small>PREVIOUS LESSON</small>
								<strong>Combined Volume</strong>
							</div>
						</a>

						<a href="/surface-areas-and-volumes/pyqs" class="next-lesson">
							<div>
								<small>NEXT LESSON</small>
								<strong>Previous Year PYQs</strong>
							</div>
							<span>→</span>
						</a>
					</div>
				</article>

				<!-- SIDEBAR -->
				<aside class="lesson-sidebar">
					<div class="sidebar-card">
						<div class="sidebar-title">SURFACE AREAS & VOLUMES</div>
						<div class="progress-text">Lesson 03 of 04</div>
						<div class="progress-bar">
							<div style="width: 75%;"></div>
						</div>

						<div class="sidebar-lessons">
							<a href="/surface-areas-and-volumes/surface-area-of-combined-solids" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>01</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Combined Surface Area</strong>
									<small>Exposed CSA sum rule</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/surface-areas-and-volumes/volume-of-combined-solids" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>02</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Combined Volume</strong>
									<small>Sum of volumes rule</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/surface-areas-and-volumes/applications-and-practice" class="sidebar-lesson active">
								<span>03</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Applications & Practice</strong>
									<small>NCERT word problems</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/surface-areas-and-volumes/pyqs" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>04</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Previous Year PYQs</strong>
									<small>CBSE 2020-2024 practice set</small>
								</div>
							</a>
						</div>
					</div>
				</aside>
			</section>
		</div>
	</main>

	<style>
		.lesson-page {
